            <div xml:id="d13">

                <pb facs="0102" n="12" sameAs="frus:frus1920v02/pg12"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">837.00/1670: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Cuba</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >White</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Habana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-05-23T15:00:00-05:29"><hi rendition="#italic">May 23, 1920—3
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 4:59 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>117. Conservatives this morning nominated without opposition Rafael Montalvo as
                    presidential candidate. Selection of vice-president <pb facs="0103" n="13"
                        xml:id="pg13"/> postponed pending agreement with Zayas coalitionists who
                    will probably be permitted to name candidate. Major Stephenson requests General
                    Crowder be notified.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">White</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
